Z||000000||Dan Robinson||11-01-2001||08:21 PM||||I can't get the fuel rail off of my 2.8.  What am I doing wrong?  It won't budge.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||11-01-2001||08:58 PM||||You need to remove the two bolts holding it down; the fuel lines and the cold start injector line. You then rock it back and forth until it comes loose.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||11-01-2001||09:06 PM||||And spray the holes with WD40. The O-rings tend to bond to the lower intake.||||reg||1
Z||000003||beer_stud_21||11-01-2001||09:53 PM||||And.... If brute force doesn't work: You need a bigger brute.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>-Marlin||||reg||1
